    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d1622">

                <pb facs="1018" n="902" xml:id="pg902"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">File No. 811.0144/9.</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Secretary of State to
                        Consul Garrett.</hi>
                </head>
                <opener>
                    <seg rendition="#center">[Telegram.]</seg>
                </opener>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Department of State</hi>, <lb/>
                            <hi rendition="#italic">Washington</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1914-01-29T18:00:00-05:00">
                            <hi rendition="#italic">January 29, 1914, 6 p.m.</hi>
                        </date>
                    </dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>Renew to appropriate authorities demand for release of Cantu and intimate that
                    unless this demand is immediately complied with, this Government will find it
                    necessary to consider drastic measures in the premises.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Bryan</hi></signed>.</closer>
            </div>
        </body>
